  "final_text": "**Proposed disposition:** ESCALATE (confidence 0.70). It is recorded as a proposal, case C-A-261028-0010, awaiting a human decision.\n\n**Three facts that drove it:**\n1. The trader placed a one-sided SELL limit of 31,395, which is 12.9 times average depth and 3 ticks from the touch. It had no fills and was fully cancelled.\n2. While it rested, the trader bought 1,053 by market order. The SELL was cancelled 158 ms later, and the price reverted 2.5 ticks after the cancel. The favourable move before the buy was only +0.5 tick.\n3. No legitimate explanation is supported. The trader is a market maker but is registered only on SYN.B, not SYN.A. There was no two-sided quoting, no public event and no risk event.\n\n**What would change my mind:** evidence that the SELL was a genuine working order or a quote, or that the BUY belonged to an unrelated client or parent order. A longer-frame review showing repeated cycles would raise this to DRAFT_STOR. This was a single cycle, so I did not propose a STOR draft.",
